{"name":"Abbey Stone","hex":"#aba798","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"abbey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The office or dominion of an abbot or abbess. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A monastery or society of people, secluded from the world and devoted to religion and celibacy, which is headed by an abbot or abbess; also, the monastic building or buildings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abbey"},{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abbey","blocks":[{"text":"An abbey is a type of monastery used by members of a religious order under the governance of an abbot or abbess. Abbeys provide a complex of buildings and land for religious activities, work, and housing of Christian or Buddhist monks and nuns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Senanquecloister.jpg/330px-Senanquecloister.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbey"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Abad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG/500px-Abad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Abad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG/1280px-Abad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Abad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG/500px-Abad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Church of the former Bath Abbey, Somerset","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbad%C3%ADa_de_Bath%2C_Bath%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-12%2C_DD_07.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Church_of_Naantali_inside_2.jpg/500px-Church_of_Naantali_inside_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Church_of_Naantali_inside_2.jpg/1280px-Church_of_Naantali_inside_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Church_of_Naantali_inside_2.jpg/500px-Church_of_Naantali_inside_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An interior of the Bridgettine